From ac03087a314c3f14e6337e764530324f396fab70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 11:27:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(2d): enter the first tabbed contour level where the
 levels above cut

The untabbed levels of a tabbed ring now start where the first window of
its tabbed levels begins (tab_clear::level_start). So the first tabbed
window dives into the kerf and the lead-in that each level above cut, one
stepdown or less below their floor, and not 18 mm into uncut sheet. The
tab layout does not change. A ring that shares a level with another ring
or band keeps its seam, so coincident cuts split at the same point.

The later tab windows still dive at lead-in starts that no level above
cut (#3678); the verifier law is #3679.

Pinned by crates/motion/tests/contour_tab_entry.rs. The catalog case
2d/contour-tabs is regenerated.

Fixes #3453

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
